# Compliance

This directory holds tax filings, state filings, and audit reports for
{{ org_name }} (EIN: {{ ein }}).

## What belongs here

- Federal tax filings (e.g. Form 990 and its schedules).
- {{ state }} state filings — annual reports, charitable-solicitation
  registrations, and any other required state compliance documents.
{%- if federal_grants_focus %}
- Single Audit reports and other artifacts required by 2 CFR 200 Subpart F
  once the Corporation's federal expenditures exceed the applicable
  threshold (see `bylaws.md`{% if not include_bylaws_example %}, if adopted{% endif %}, Article XI, Section 11.3).
{%- endif %}
- Independent audit reports and management letters, if your organization
  obtains them.

## How compliance artifacts get here

Filed and finalized compliance documents are added through this
repository's ordinary governance process (see `GOVERNANCE.md`): typically
{{ "an" if vcs_platform == "gitlab" else "a" }} {{ mr_term }} on an `admin/`
branch, since these are records of filings already made rather than
matters requiring a fresh board vote — unless your Delegation of Authority
Policy requires board approval before filing, in which case use a
`board/` branch instead.

## A note on privacy

This directory is a scaffold. It ships empty. Tax and state filings
combine your organization's EIN with financial detail and, on some forms,
individual compensation figures for directors, officers, and key
employees — information that is sensitive even though parts of a Form 990
are separately required to be publicly disclosed by the IRS.

**Your organization controls its own privacy posture for its rendered
repository**, independent of what the IRS separately requires you to
disclose elsewhere. If this repository is public, or you are otherwise
unsure whether a specific filing is appropriate for this level of
visibility, keep it in your organization's own **private** repository
instead.

**Never contribute real compliance filings, or any other real adopted
content, back to the [Golden Records](https://github.com/USCouncil/golden-records)
commons.** That repository is a public, generic template — it must never
receive real organization data, including a real EIN. This directory, in
*your own* rendered repository, is the right place for your real filings;
the commons template is not.
